> I have a single-volume domain 18G. I want to shrink it to create a new
> raw partition(not to join any domain). how do i do that ?
> I am preparing a OS upgrade, the purpose of my request is to backup
> existing data to the spare partition and restore if the upgrade fail.
> 
> v5.1 using AdvFS.
> 
> thanks,
> 
> James.Q.L

If you have another disk or partition (and AdvFS license for 
addvol/rmvol), then addvol of the new smaller partition (or 
several partitions to get enough space), then rmvol the 18GB disk.

AdvFS will on-line migrate all the data off of the 18GB disk and 
put it on the added volume(s).

Then reconfigure the 18GB disk and addvol in the new home, and 
rmvol the temporary volumes you no longer want to use.

If you do not have the space, then vdump/vrestore are the next 
best options.

                                        Bob Harris


