I do not understand your question.

The raw partitions are always available.  Assuming Tru64 5.*, then 
if this is a simple disk, then /dev/disk/dsk* for the block device 
and /dev/rdisk/dsk* for the raw partitions.  If this is a LSM 
volume then the are somewhere under /dev/...

The showfdmn command will tell you want partitions make up the 
domain.

If you wish to actually destroy the AdvFS file system, then you 
can rmfdmn.

If you have _NOT_ destroyed the AdvFS domain, but you are booting 
up a different OS, you can use advscan to import AdvFS volumes 
into Tru64 UNIX.

